Administrative tasks - dail tasks the admin performs. Updating SCCM and assigning admin roles

Four sub categories:

1) Role-based Administration

- Sccm gives you 15 roles that you can assign to users that will limit their permissions to only accomplish the tasks they are qualified to complete. 

Example The full administrator role allows an admin full access while a read only analyst has read only access.



2) Remote MANAGEMENT 

- This allows remote control of Sccm clients.

You can use remote control to troubleshoot hardware and software configuration issues.

To configure remote control, open the default client settings, click Remote tools, click configure

settings and complete the setup.

3) In-Console Updates

- Sccm provides an automated method to find and install recommended updates for your

configuration manager infrastructure.

4) Monitoring

- If you need information, open monitoring if you need to troubleshoot your Sccm infrastructure monitoring

is a good place to start.

- There are 22 different functions, including client health reporting, queries, alerts, deployments

and many others.

Monitoring is the first place to go if you need to troubleshoot your Sccm environment.

